# NATHAN TABOR 3-D PRINT SHOP — FIVE MATRIX
This directory contains the **original full 22,785-byte standalone browser simulator** from the conversation export, copied unchanged to `index.html`.

## Launch points
- ONE: `app-factory/one/index.html`
- Factory website: `app-factory/index.html`
- Nathan AI main hub: `app-factory/nathan-ai/index.html`
- Nathan AI websites: `app-factory/nathan-ai/websites/index.html`
- Original artifacts hub: `app-factory/one/restored/index.html`

## What's real and what is simulated
The browser's canvas state, animation loop, inspector, control events, UI, JSON export and voxel state are actual running code. Five printing cells, Gopher/ant scouts, resource acquisition, printheads, fabrication and convergence into ONE are **software simulations**. No actual NASA or physical printer is connected. The sample print path is illustrative and MUST NOT be sent to hardware as G-code.

## Preserve the original
Do not overwrite or paraphrase this `index.html` in later versions. Add new modules alongside the source. Do not silently change the five matrix names, user terminology or visual composition.
- Source: user-supplied project built earlier in this conversation.
- No real hardware authorization, fabrication-ready machine file or private credentials included.
- There is no external crawler; the gopher scouts use curated source references.

## Testing
The inline JavaScript was syntax checked with Node v22 (`node --check`). Headless chromium loading is blocked in this workspace; a browser-level integration QA run must occur in an unrestricted development environment. Node/source integrity tests are provided in `test.mjs`.
